<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccccc} {9}{x}\amp+\amp{4}{y}\amp+\amp{5}{z}\amp+\amp{78}{w}\amp-\amp{55}{v}\amp=\amp{62}\\-{2}{x}\amp-\amp{2}{y}\amp-\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{44}{w}\amp+\amp{10}{v}\amp=\amp-{46}\\{6}{x}\amp-\amp{9}{y}\amp+\amp{3}{z}\amp+\amp{15}{w}\amp-\amp{141}{v}\amp=\amp{27}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
v = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{2}-{4}{w}+{9}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{1}-{3}{w}-{9}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{8}-{6}{w}+{2}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{v}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

